{
  "dom_id": "step-q211472",
  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $2÷\\frac{6}{7}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{6}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{6}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2}{1}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6} & =\\frac{2}{6}\\times \\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\times 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert our result to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
